.TH CLAUDE-SESSION 1 "2026-08-01" "claude-session-management" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-session \- star, move, and delete Claude Code sessions from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-session
.I operation
.RI [ args " ...]"
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
claude\-session list                  \fR# every project, grouped\fP
claude\-session star 4bdd76            \fR# star a session in the current project\fP
claude\-session \-i                     \fR# interactive fzf browser\fP
claude\-session mv 4bdd76 ~/old ~/new  \fR# move a session between projects\fP
claude\-session rm 4bdd76              \fR# delete a session (asks first)\fP
claude\-session export \-\-all \-o bak.tar.gz  \fR# back up everything\fP
claude\-session import bak.tar.gz      \fR# restore from an archive\fP
.EE
.in
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-session
manages the session files Claude Code keeps under
.IR ~/.claude/projects/ .
Starring drops a star into a session's title so it stands out in the
.B /resume
picker \(em there is no separate database, the star rides along on the
session's
.B .jsonl
file itself, which means it travels automatically on
.B mv
and disappears on
.BR rm .
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.BI "list " "[path]"
List sessions. With no path, every project is listed, grouped by project.
With a path, only that project's sessions are listed. Alias:
.BR ls .
.TP
.BI "project " "subcommand" " [args ...]"
Manage whole projects. Alias:
.BR proj .
The subcommands are:
.RS
.TP
.B ls
List every project with its session count. Alias:
.BR list .
.TP
.BI "mv " "[\-f|\-\-force] from-path to-path"
Move a whole project's sessions to another path. If the destination
project already exists, sessions are merged in. A filename collision
(rare \(em session filenames are Claude Code's own random UUIDs) prompts
per file to
.BR o verwrite,
overwrite
.BR a ll,
.BR s kip,
or skip a\fBl\fRl, unless
.B \-f
/
.B \-\-force
is given, which overwrites every collision without asking. Alias:
.BR move .
.TP
.BI "rm " "[\-f|\-\-force] [path]"
Delete a whole project and all of its sessions. Asks for confirmation
unless
.B \-f
/
.B \-\-force
is given. Aliases:
.BR delete ", " remove .
.TP
.BI "export " "[path] [\-o out]"
Export every session in a project to an archive. With no path, the current
directory's project is used. See
.B export
below for archive formats.
.RE
.TP
.BI "star " "session-id-or-partial" " [path]"
Star a session so it shows a star in
.BR /resume .
.TP
.BI "unstar " "session-id-or-partial" " [path]"
Remove a session's star.
.TP
.BI "\-i " "[path]"
Interactively browse sessions with fzf and act on the selection. Each row
shows the session's last-modified time, the context-window tokens it was
last using, its on-disk size, and its title.
.B tab
multi-selects;
.B enter
toggles the star on everything selected, while
.B ctrl-x
(or
.BR del )
deletes the selection after a confirmation. The list reopens after each
action, so you can star, unstar, and delete repeatedly until you quit with
.B esc
or
.BR q .
.TP
.BI "mv " "session-id-or-partial from-path to-path"
Move a single session from one project path to another. Alias:
.BR move .
.TP
.BI "rm " "[\-f|\-\-force] session-id-or-partial" " [path]"
Delete a session. Asks for confirmation unless
.B \-f
/
.B \-\-force
is given. Aliases:
.BR delete ", " remove .
.TP
.BI "rm-untitled " "[\-f|\-\-force] [path]"
Delete every untitled session. With no path, all projects are scanned;
with a path, only that project. Asks for confirmation unless
.B \-f
/
.B \-\-force
is given. Alias:
.BR clean-untitled .
.TP
.BI "export " "session-id-or-partial" " [path] [\-o out]"
Export a single session to an archive (default
.IR claude-sessions-<timestamp>.tar.gz ).
To export a whole project, use
.BR "project export" .
.TP
.BI "export \-\-all " "[\-o out]"
Export every session in every project.
.TP
.BI "import " "archive" " [\-\-to path] [\-f]"
Import sessions from an archive produced by
.BR export .
Each session is restored to the project it was exported from, unless
.B \-\-to
redirects them all to one project. A session conflicts when a
.I .jsonl
with the same session ID already exists in the destination project; by
default the conflicting session is skipped and the existing one is left
untouched. Pass
.B \-f
to overwrite conflicting sessions with the archived copy instead. The
closing summary reports how many sessions were imported and how many
were skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit. Alias:
.BR \-v .
.TP
.B help
Show a usage summary. Aliases:
.BR "-h" ", " "--help" .
Also shown when no operation is given.
.SH ARCHIVES
Archive format is chosen by the output filename: anything ending in
.B .zip
uses
.B zip
/
.BR unzip ,
otherwise the archive is a
.B .tar.gz
built with
.BR tar .
Both are shelled out to as ambient system tools.
.SH SESSION IDS
Any unique substring of a session's id works anywhere a
.I session-id-or-partial
is expected \(em there is no need to type the whole UUID. An ambiguous or
missing match prints a diagnostic and exits non-zero.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Node.js >= 14. The interactive mode
.RB ( "\-i" )
additionally needs
.BR fzf (1)
on PATH; export/import need
.BR tar (1)
or
.BR zip (1) / unzip (1)
depending on the chosen archive format.
.SH CAVEATS
A running Claude Code session caches its own title in memory, so starring
the session you're currently in won't show the star in
.B /resume
until Claude Code reloads.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.claude/projects/<encoded-path>/<session-id>.jsonl
.RS
One file per session.
.I <encoded-path>
is the project's absolute path with every
.B /
replaced by
.BR \- .
The filename base is the session's id and is never changed by any
operation here.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fzf (1),
.BR tar (1)
.br
Project homepage: https://github.com/wilversings/claude-session-management
